layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | A
    strong project
    | is a repository on the factory. It owns its packages for life, its settings and its history, and it says where its
    a(href="/docs/line") line
    | runs: on which paired machine, from which checkout, with which line file. Open
    strong Projects
    | in the top bar (on a phone, go to
    code {{ site.url }}/projects
    | ).
  h2#what What a project holds
  dl
    dt
      | Key
    dd
      | A short name such as
      code shop-api
      | : a lower-case letter, then letters, digits and dashes, 2 to 24 characters. It never changes; tools and links use it.
    dt
      | Name and repository
    dd
      | A display name, and the GitHub repository (
      code owner/name
      | ) when there is one. One project per repository.
    dt
      | Id prefix
    dd
      | Optional, such as
      code SH-
      | : the package ids the project owns (see
      a(href="#ids") Package ids
      | ).
    dt
      | Machine and main checkout
    dd
      | Where the line runs: a paired machine with a
      a(href="/docs/runner") runner
      | , and the trusted main checkout of the repository on it. The runner reads the line file there, never in a worker's worktree.
    dt
      | Line file
    dd
      | The path of the line file relative to the checkout,
      code factory.json
      | by default (
      a(href="/docs/line") The line
      | ).
    dt
      | State and autopilot
    dd
      | Active, paused or archived (
      a(href="#states") States
      | ), and whether the
      a(href="/docs/autopilot") autopilot
      | moves its packages along the line.
  p
    | A package belongs to one project for life. Packages without a project (older data, one-off tasks) still work on the
    a(href="/docs/backlog") backlog
    | as before.
  h2#put-on Putting a repo on the factory
  p
    | Before you start, the machine must be
    a(href="/docs/machines") paired
    | and run a
    a(href="/docs/runner") runner
    | whose allowed folders include the checkout and the folder where package worktrees go (by default next to the checkout:
    code ../<checkout folder>-wt/
    | ). Then pick one of these:
  ul
    li
      strong In Claude Code
      | , in the repository:
      code /buildyboy:factory-init
      | . It reads the repository, proposes a
      code factory.json
      | , checks it, adds the package folder and a template, and registers the project, or prints a prefilled link to the form below (
      a(href="/docs/skills#factory-init") Skills
      | ).
    li
      strong From the Projects page
      | : under the factory projects, each repository Buildyboy has seen in your sessions but that has no project yet has a
      strong Put on the factory
      | button. It opens the new-project form filled in from that checkout.
    li
      strong New project
      | at the top of the Projects page opens the same form empty. The form also reads its fields from the address, so
      code /projects/new?key=shop-api&name=Shop%20API&repo=acme/shop-api&machineId=…&checkout=…&lineFile=factory.json&idPrefix=SH-
      | opens it filled in.
    li
      strong An operator bot
      | can create it with
      code projects_save
      | (
      a(href="/docs/operators") Operators
      | ).
  p
    | Then commit the line file on the base branch and press
    strong Check setup
    | on the project's Setup tab: the runner reads the line, validates it and reports what it resolved to. Only you (on the web) or an operator token may set a project's machine, checkout and line file, because they decide what the runner executes.
  h2#ids Package ids
  ul
    li
      | Ids stay unique across all projects. A project with an id prefix owns the ids that start with it: a package created in it as
      code P1
      | is stored as
      code SH-P1
      | , and one created without an id gets the next number,
      code SH-7
      | . An id that already starts with the prefix is kept.
    li
      | The id without the prefix is the
      strong local id
      | (
      code P1
      | ). Package files, the planner and dependencies use local ids:
      code depends_on: [P1]
      | in project shop-api means
      code SH-P1
      | .
    li
      | The prefix is fixed once the project has packages. A project without a prefix keeps ids as given.
    li
      | Line files use both:
      code {id}
      | (
      code SH-P1
      | ) and
      code {localId}
      | (
      code P1
      | ), also in lower case (
      code {idLower}
      | ,
      code {localIdLower}
      | ), for branches, folders and database names (
      a(href="/docs/line#placeholders") Placeholders
      | ).
  h2#states Pause, archive and delete
  dl
    dt
      | Active
    dd
      | Normal.
    dt
      | Paused
    dd
      strong Pause
      | on the project page. Nothing new starts: no claim, no launch, and the autopilot leaves the project alone. Work already in flight carries on.
      strong Resume
      | undoes it.
    dt
      | Archived
    dd
      strong Archive…
      | on the project page, after a confirmation. The project and its open packages leave the default lists, and nothing in it can be claimed or launched.
      strong Unarchive
      | brings back the project and exactly the packages archiving put away. Archived projects sit behind
      strong Show archived
      | on the Projects page.
    dt
      | Deleted
    dd
      strong Delete project…
      | at the bottom of the Setup tab, only while the project has no packages.
  h2#archive The archive
  p
    | Integrated packages do not stay on the board forever. A package is
    strong archived
    | when:
  ul
    li
      | it was integrated more than a day ago (the delay is
      strong archive_done_after_hours
      | in
      a(href="/docs/settings") Settings
      | , 24 by default; 0 turns the sweep off);
    li
      | you press
      strong Archive done
      | on a project's Done tab, or archive it from its package page;
    li
      | its project is archived;
    li
      | an operator archives it (
      code tasks_update {archived: true}
      | ).
  p
    | The board and
    code tasks_list
    | leave archived packages out, so the
    strong Integrată
    | column holds what landed in the last day. The project's
    strong Done
    | tab is its archive: every integrated package with its date, rounds, cost and duration. Opening an archived package, and dependencies on it, work as before. Unarchiving a package puts it back on the board.
  h2#list The Projects page
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="projects-desktop.png" alt="The Projects page on a desktop: a card for Shop API with autopilot on, a progress bar, packages on the line and one waiting on you; a card for Billing, paused; then other repositories with a Put on the factory button." caption="Factory projects first, then the repositories that are not on the factory yet.")
  p
    | Factory projects come first, active ones before paused ones. Each card shows the autopilot state, a progress bar (integrated packages of all its packages), what is on the line, what waits on you (blocked packages and pending decisions), the cost so far and the last activity. Tap a card to open the project.
  p
    | Below them,
    strong Other repositories
    | lists every repository Buildyboy has seen in your sessions that has no factory project, each with
    strong Put on the factory
    | .
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="projects-phone.png" alt="The Projects page on a phone: the project cards stacked, then the list of other repositories." caption="On a phone the cards stack." phone)
  h2#page A project's page
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="project-desktop.png" alt="A project page on a desktop: the header with the Autopilot switch and the Pause and Archive buttons, the progress and cost figures, the tabs Line, Backlog, Done, Activity and Setup, then two packages on the line and a pending decision." caption="A project with autopilot on: what is on the line and what waits on you.")
  p
    | The header holds the project's switches:
    strong Autopilot
    | (
    a(href="/docs/autopilot") Autopilot
    | ),
    strong Pause
    | or
    strong Resume
    | ,
    strong Archive…
    | or
    strong Unarchive
    | , and
    strong Plan new work
    | , which asks the
    a(href="/docs/planning") planner
    | for a plan from a goal you type. Under it: progress, cost, decisions waiting and the last activity. The tabs:
  dl
    dt
      | Line
    dd
      | The packages in flight, each with a stage stepper (prepare, qa, build, G1 to G5, cleanup), the worker's lamp and what it waits for; the project's pending decisions; the ready packages that start next.
    dt
      | Backlog
    dd
      | This project's board, the same as the
      a(href="/docs/backlog") backlog
      | filtered to it.
    dt
      | Done
    dd
      | The archive: integrated packages with date, rounds, cost and duration, and
      strong Archive done
      | for the integrated ones still on the board.
    dt
      | Activity
    dd
      | The sessions, pull requests, commits and cost of the project's checkouts (see
      a(href="#checkouts") below
      | ).
    dt
      | Setup
    dd
      | Name, key, repository and id prefix; where the line runs (machine, main checkout, line file); the resolved line as the runner last reported it, with
      strong Check setup
      | to ask again; and overrides that win over the line file: parallel packages (
      code limits.workers
      | ), gate rounds (
      code limits.rounds
      | ), the model per role, and when to ask before G5 (
      code integrate.approval
      | ). A project that came from the old per-repo factory settings also shows its allocation (worktree, ports, database prefix, migrations, cleanup lines) until its line file declares its own resources.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="project-phone.png" alt="A project page on a phone: the header with its switches, then the tabs and the line." caption="The same project on a phone." phone)
  h2#checkouts Repositories seen by telemetry
  p
    | Separately from factory projects, Buildyboy groups every session by the folder it ran in, by itself, as sessions arrive:
  ul
    li
      | A session belongs to the
      strong git repository
      | it runs in (its top folder), even when Claude started in a sub-folder; outside git, to the folder Claude started in.
    li
      | The same repository on two machines is two checkouts, one per machine. This includes Windows and WSL on the same computer.
    li
      | Repositories on github.com are linked to their GitHub page, which lets Buildyboy follow pull requests once you add a
      a(href="/docs/settings#github") GitHub token
      | .
  p
    | A factory project links to the checkouts of its repository, and its
    strong Activity
    | tab shows them: daily cost, recent sessions, jobs that ran there, pull requests with their checks, commits made during sessions and the latest progress notes of
    a(href="/docs/composer#harness") harness runs
    | . There is nothing to create or delete for a checkout. The Floor's
    strong All projects
    | filter shows one checkout's sessions.
